# Distribution for CommonsLang_Rust (Linux_x86)

Builds the Rust toolchain objects for the `Linux_x86` slot and proves them by building a
static library that uses ring's C and assembly. It runs on a `Linux_x86_64` host.

## rustc, cargo and the host standard library

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Host.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/host-Linux_x86_64 slot=Release.Linux_x86_64
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86_64", value-id: "ombmr27wwnww6srfwslaojl3ym53vy22x44xmiipldri2fvrhbfcq")\;

## The standard library for the target

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Std.Files@1.99.1 -d ${RUNTIME}/std slot=Release.Linux_x86
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86", value-id: "o3rk5rrp4d3quuw2hidrlqgsckdapeucgs4z2scgwzlruyx4ux55a")\;

## The CargoLock dialog (author time)

Ships the `CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Bundle` dialog, which writes a crates bundle from a
`Cargo.lock`.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.CargoLock.Export@1.0.0 -f ${RUNTIME}/CargoLock.Export.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86_64", value-id: "ob5a6ojnxcmkjcg52pjpfevzbwbyzfz5wb5yowawfdpvffzjbqbia")\;

## Usage: a static library that uses ring

`assets/fixture/ring` is a Cargo workspace whose `ringlib` crate calls ring's SHA-256.
Its crates bundle came from the CargoLock dialog. cargo builds it offline.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_Rust.Cargo.F_StaticLib@1.0.0 -d ${RUNTIME}/ringlib
  >   modver=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.RingLib@1.0.0
  >   srcasset=CommonsLang_Rust.Apparatus.RingFixture@1.0.0 srcpath=assets/fixture/ring
  >   crates=CommonsLang_Rust.Fixture.Crates.Bundle@1.0.0 package=ringlib
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86", value-id: "oq7fjq6rgfrzs4iht2fqjqxcseknak7sxml352e37ybyony7u7vua")\;
